/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 1 Kings chapters 6-10
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("1kings", [
{n:6, name:"The Temple Built", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 6:13",verse:"And I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will not forsake my people Israel."}, facts:["Did you know the temple stones were shaped off site, so there was neither hammer nor axe nor any tool of iron heard in the house while it was being built (1 Kings 6:7)?","Did you know the work began in the four hundred and eightieth year after Israel came out of Egypt, in the fourth year of Solomon's reign, in the month Zif, and took seven years to finish (1 Kings 6:1, 6:38)?","Did you know the two cherubims of olive wood stood ten cubits high, with wings stretching from wall to wall and touching each other in the midst of the oracle (1 Kings 6:23-27)?"], questions:[
{q:"When did Solomon begin to build the house of the LORD?", options:["In the 480th year after Israel left Egypt, in the fourth year of his reign","In the 40th year of the wilderness wandering","In the second year of David's reign","In the first year after the temple of Moses was moved"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:1",verse:"And it came to pass in the four hundred and eightieth year after the children of Israel were come out of the land of Egypt, in the fourth year of Solomon’s reign over Israel, in the month Zif, which is the second month, that he began to build the house of the LORD.", insight:"God dates His work by redemption; the temple begins where the exodus left off, 480 years on."},
{q:"What month was named for the start of the building?", options:["Zif, the second month","Ethanim, the seventh month","Abib, the first month","Bul, the eighth month"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:1",verse:"And it came to pass in the four hundred and eightieth year after the children of Israel were come out of the land of Egypt, in the fourth year of Solomon’s reign over Israel, in the month Zif, which is the second month, that he began to build the house of the LORD.", insight:"The month is named in Scripture; God keeps careful records of when His house is begun."},
{q:"What were the length, breadth, and height of the house Solomon built for the LORD?", options:["Threescore cubits long, twenty broad, thirty high","Forty cubits long, twenty broad, twenty high","A hundred cubits long, fifty broad, thirty high","Twenty cubits long, twenty broad, twenty high"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:2",verse:"And the house which king Solomon built for the LORD, the length thereof was threescore cubits, and the breadth thereof twenty cubits, and the height thereof thirty cubits.", insight:"Every cubit is measured; God is served by exact obedience, not vague devotion."},
{q:"How large was the porch before the temple?", options:["Twenty cubits long and ten cubits broad","Thirty cubits long and fifteen broad","Forty cubits long and twenty broad","Ten cubits long and five broad"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:3",verse:"And the porch before the temple of the house, twenty cubits was the length thereof, according to the breadth of the house; and ten cubits was the breadth thereof before the house.", insight:"Even the entrance was planned; approach to God is never an afterthought."},
{q:"What kind of windows were made for the house?", options:["Windows of narrow lights","Great windows of open lattice","Round windows of brass","Windows shuttered with cedar"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:4",verse:"And for the house he made windows of narrow lights.", insight:"Narrow lights for a house of glory; God's presence needs no glaring spectacle."},
{q:"What was built against the walls of the house round about?", options:["Chambers, against both the temple and the oracle","A wall of brass ten cubits thick","Stables for the king's horses","Storehouses for the tribute gold"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:5",verse:"And against the wall of the house he built chambers round about, against the walls of the house round about, both of the temple and of the oracle: and he made chambers round about:", insight:"The holy place was ringed with service rooms; worship and work belong side by side."},
{q:"How broad were the three stories of side chambers?", options:["Five, six, and seven cubits, from lowest to highest","Four cubits each, all alike","Ten, eight, and six cubits","Three, four, and five cubits"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:6",verse:"The nethermost chamber was five cubits broad, and the middle was six cubits broad, and the third was seven cubits broad: for without in the wall of the house he made narrowed rests round about, that the beams should not be fastened in the walls of the house.", insight:"Each story had its own measure; growth in God's house happens level by level."},
{q:"Why were no beams fastened into the walls of the house?", options:["Narrowed rests were made in the wall, so the beams rested without being fastened in","The builders forgot to cut the sockets","The walls were too thin to hold them","The cedar beams were too short"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:6",verse:"The nethermost chamber was five cubits broad, and the middle was six cubits broad, and the third was seven cubits broad: for without in the wall of the house he made narrowed rests round about, that the beams should not be fastened in the walls of the house.", insight:"The beams rested without piercing the walls; strength that does not wound is wisdom."},
{q:"What sound was never heard in the house while it was being built?", options:["Neither hammer nor axe nor any tool of iron","The voices of the workmen","The sawing of cedar","The songs of the Levites"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:7",verse:"And the house, when it was in building, was built of stone made ready before it was brought thither: so that there was neither hammer nor axe nor any tool of iron heard in the house, while it was in building.", insight:"The stone came ready, the house rose in quiet; God builds His greatest works without noise."},
{q:"How did one go up from the middle chamber to the third?", options:["By winding stairs, entering through a door on the right side","By a ladder of bronze","Through a trapdoor in the ceiling","By steps cut into the outer wall"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:8",verse:"The door for the middle chamber was in the right side of the house: and they went up with winding stairs into the middle chamber, and out of the middle into the third.", insight:"Winding stairs upward; the way higher in God's house is steady, turning, patient ascent."},
{q:"With what was the house covered when its frame was finished?", options:["With beams and boards of cedar","With tiles of baked clay","With plates of hammered gold","With skins of badgers"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:9",verse:"So he built the house, and finished it; and covered the house with beams and boards of cedar.", insight:"Cedar above all; God covers His house with what is fragrant and enduring."},
{q:"What condition did God set before keeping His word to David?", options:["Walk in His statutes, execute His judgments, keep His commandments","Offer a thousand burnt offerings each year","Build a house twice as large","Bring all the nations to Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:12",verse:"Concerning this house which thou art in building, if thou wilt walk in my statutes, and execute my judgments, and keep all my commandments to walk in them; then will I perform my word with thee, which I spake unto David thy father:", insight:"The promise stands, but the blessing walks with obedience; God asks for the heart, not just the building."},
{q:"What did God promise Solomon concerning the house?", options:["I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will not forsake my people Israel","I will move the ark to a greater temple","I will make Jerusalem the only city on earth","I will speak from the oracle forevermore"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:13",verse:"And I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will not forsake my people Israel.", insight:"The promise is presence, not property; God commits Himself to dwell, not merely to visit."},
{q:"With what were the inner walls and floor of the house lined?", options:["Walls with boards of cedar, floor with planks of fir","Walls with marble, floor with brass","Walls with tapestries, floor with carpets","Walls with gold leaf, floor with silver"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:15",verse:"And he built the walls of the house within with boards of cedar, both the floor of the house, and the walls of the cieling: and he covered them on the inside with wood, and covered the floor of the house with planks of fir.", insight:"Cedar within, fir beneath; the inside of God's house was as carefully made as the outside."},
{q:"How long was the temple proper, before the oracle?", options:["Forty cubits","Thirty cubits","Twenty cubits","Sixty cubits"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:17",verse:"And the house, that is, the temple before it, was forty cubits long.", insight:"Forty cubits of holy space before the most holy; God leads us deeper by degrees."},
{q:"What carving covered the cedar within, so that no stone was seen?", options:["Knops and open flowers","Lions and eagles","Vines and pomegranates","Serpents and stars"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:18",verse:"And the cedar of the house within was carved with knops and open flowers: all was cedar; there was no stone seen.", insight:"Flowers carved where no stone showed; beauty in God's house serves no use but His delight."},
{q:"What were the dimensions of the oracle, and with what was it overlaid?", options:["Twenty cubits each way, overlaid with pure gold","Thirty cubits each way, overlaid with brass","Ten cubits each way, overlaid with silver","Forty cubits each way, left as bare stone"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:20",verse:"And the oracle in the forepart was twenty cubits in length, and twenty cubits in breadth, and twenty cubits in the height thereof: and he overlaid it with pure gold; and so covered the altar which was of cedar.", insight:"A perfect cube of gold; the holiest place is measured in perfection, not convenience."},
{q:"What did Solomon make within the oracle, and of what wood?", options:["Two cherubims of olive tree, each ten cubits high","Two lions of cedar, each five cubits high","Four pillars of fir","A veil of blue and purple"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:23",verse:"And within the oracle he made two cherubims of olive tree, each ten cubits high.", insight:"Olive wood cherubims, ten cubits tall; guardians of the presence, carved from the tree of peace."},
{q:"How far did one cherub's wings reach from tip to tip?", options:["Ten cubits, five cubits per wing","Twenty cubits, ten per wing","Five cubits altogether","Fifteen cubits, seven and a half per wing"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:24",verse:"And five cubits was the one wing of the cherub, and five cubits the other wing of the cherub: from the uttermost part of the one wing unto the uttermost part of the other were ten cubits.", insight:"Ten cubits of outstretched wing; heaven's guardians cover exactly the space God gives them."},
{q:"How many years was Solomon in building the house?", options:["Seven years","Three years","Eleven years","Thirteen years"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 6:38",verse:"And in the eleventh year, in the month Bul, which is the eighth month, was the house finished throughout all the parts thereof, and according to all the fashion of it. So was he seven years in building it.", insight:"Seven years for the house of God; great work for the Lord is never rushed."}
]},
{n:7, name:"The Furnishings", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 7:51",verse:"So was ended all the work that king Solomon made for the house of the LORD. And Solomon brought in the things which David his father had dedicated; even the silver, and the gold, and the vessels, did he put among the treasures of the house of the LORD."}, facts:["Did you know Solomon spent thirteen years building his own palace, nearly twice the seven years spent on the LORD's house (1 Kings 7:1)?","Did you know the master craftsman Hiram was a widow's son of the tribe of Naphtali, whose father was a Tyrian worker in brass, and he was filled with wisdom, understanding, and cunning for brass work (1 Kings 7:13-14)?","Did you know the great brass pieces were cast in the clay ground of the Jordan plain between Succoth and Zarthan, and there were so many vessels they were left unweighed (1 Kings 7:46-47)?"], questions:[
{q:"How long was Solomon building his own house?", options:["Thirteen years","Seven years","Twenty years","Four years"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:1",verse:"But Solomon was building his own house thirteen years, and he finished all his house.", insight:"Thirteen years for his own house, seven for the Lord's; check what your own calendar says about your priorities."},
{q:"What were the dimensions of the house of the forest of Lebanon?", options:["A hundred cubits long, fifty broad, thirty high, on four rows of cedar pillars","Sixty cubits long, twenty broad, thirty high","Fifty cubits long, thirty broad, twenty high","Two hundred cubits long, a hundred broad"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:2",verse:"He built also the house of the forest of Lebanon; the length thereof was an hundred cubits, and the breadth thereof fifty cubits, and the height thereof thirty cubits, upon four rows of cedar pillars, with cedar beams upon the pillars.", insight:"A palace among cedars; earthly glory is real, but it is not the temple."},
{q:"How many cedar pillars held up the house of the forest of Lebanon?", options:["Forty five, fifteen in a row","Thirty, ten in a row","Sixty, twenty in a row","Twelve, in a single row"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:3",verse:"And it was covered with cedar above upon the beams, that lay on forty five pillars, fifteen in a row.", insight:"Forty five pillars of cedar; human strength multiplies columns, God's strength needs none."},
{q:"How large was the porch of pillars?", options:["Fifty cubits long and thirty broad","Twenty cubits long and ten broad","A hundred cubits long and fifty broad","Thirty cubits long and twenty broad"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:6",verse:"And he made a porch of pillars; the length thereof was fifty cubits, and the breadth thereof thirty cubits: and the porch was before them: and the other pillars and the thick beam were before them.", insight:"Porch upon porch; the king's house opened wide, as earthly power loves to be seen."},
{q:"What was the porch of judgment?", options:["A porch for the throne where Solomon would judge, covered with cedar","The gate where criminals were executed","A court for the priests to wash","The hall where tribute was counted"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:7",verse:"Then he made a porch for the throne where he might judge, even the porch of judgment: and it was covered with cedar from one side of the floor to the other.", insight:"A throne room for judgment; every king judges, but only one Judge is perfectly just."},
{q:"For whom did Solomon also build a house like the porch?", options:["Pharaoh's daughter, whom he had taken to wife","His mother Bathsheba","The queen of Sheba","The daughter of Hiram"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:8",verse:"And his house where he dwelt had another court within the porch, which was of the like work. Solomon made also an house for Pharaoh’s daughter, whom he had taken to wife, like unto this porch.", insight:"A house for Pharaoh's daughter; alliances with Egypt would cost Solomon dearly in the end."},
{q:"What kind of stones were used, and how were they cut?", options:["Costly stones, sawed with saws, within and without, from foundation to coping","Rough fieldstones laid in mud","Bricks baked in the sun","Marble imported from Greece"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:9",verse:"All these were of costly stones, according to the measures of hewed stones, sawed with saws, within and without, even from the foundation unto the coping, and so on the outside toward the great court.", insight:"Sawed costly stones, inside and out; integrity shows in the hidden places too."},
{q:"How large were the foundation stones?", options:["Stones of ten cubits and stones of eight cubits","Stones of three cubits each","Stones of twenty cubits each","Pebbles set in mortar"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:10",verse:"And the foundation was of costly stones, even great stones, stones of ten cubits, and stones of eight cubits.", insight:"Ten and eight cubit stones; what is buried and unseen still bears all the weight."},
{q:"Whom did Solomon send for out of Tyre?", options:["Hiram, the craftsman in brass","A shipwright for the navy","An ambassador to Pharaoh","A scribe for the chronicles"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:13",verse:"And king Solomon sent and fetched Hiram out of Tyre.", insight:"The king fetched a craftsman from Tyre; God gives skill to outsiders too, and wise kings use it."},
{q:"What is told of Hiram's parentage and gift?", options:["A widow's son of Naphtali, his father a Tyrian worker in brass, filled with wisdom, understanding, and cunning in brass","A son of David's mighty men, skilled in war","A Levite trained in the tabernacle","An Egyptian learned in all wisdom"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:14",verse:"He was a widow’s son of the tribe of Naphtali, and his father was a man of Tyre, a worker in brass: and he was filled with wisdom, and understanding, and cunning to work all works in brass. And he came to king Solomon, and wrought all his work.", insight:"A widow's son, half Israelite, filled with wisdom for brass; God raises His craftsmen from unexpected homes."},
{q:"How tall were the two pillars of brass, and what was their circumference?", options:["Eighteen cubits high apiece, twelve cubits round","Ten cubits high, six round","Twenty five cubits high, fifteen round","Twelve cubits high, eight round"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:15",verse:"For he cast two pillars of brass, of eighteen cubits high apiece: and a line of twelve cubits did compass either of them about.", insight:"Eighteen cubits of brass; the pillars of God's house stand taller than any man's work."},
{q:"How high were the chapiters of molten brass on the pillars?", options:["Five cubits each","Three cubits each","Seven cubits each","Two cubits each"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:16",verse:"And he made two chapiters of molten brass, to set upon the tops of the pillars: the height of the one chapiter was five cubits, and the height of the other chapiter was five cubits:", insight:"Five cubits of chapiter; crowning work takes its own measure of care."},
{q:"What were the two pillars named?", options:["The right Jachin and the left Boaz","The right Strength and the left Beauty","The right David and the left Solomon","The right Mercy and the left Truth"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:21",verse:"And he set up the pillars in the porch of the temple: and he set up the right pillar, and called the name thereof Jachin: and he set up the left pillar, and he called the name thereof Boaz.", insight:"Jachin, He shall establish, and Boaz, In Him is strength; the pillars preach the sermon."},
{q:"What were the size and capacity of the molten sea?", options:["Ten cubits brim to brim, five high, thirty round, holding two thousand baths","Twenty cubits across, holding five thousand baths","Five cubits across, holding five hundred baths","Fifteen cubits across, holding a thousand baths"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:23",verse:"And he made a molten sea, ten cubits from the one brim to the other: it was round all about, and his height was five cubits: and a line of thirty cubits did compass it round about.", insight:"Two thousand baths of water for cleansing; God's house always makes much room for washing."},
{q:"Upon what did the molten sea stand?", options:["Twelve oxen, three facing each direction of the compass","Twelve lions of brass","Four pillars of cedar","A single great stone"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:25",verse:"It stood upon twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, and three looking toward the west, and three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east: and the sea was set above upon them, and all their hinder parts were inward.", insight:"Twelve oxen facing every wind; cleansing in God's house faces all the world."},
{q:"How thick was the sea, and how was its brim wrought?", options:["An hand breadth thick, the brim like a cup with flowers of lilies","Two hand breadths thick, plain and unadorned","A finger thick, edged with gold","A cubit thick, carved with lions"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:26",verse:"And it was an hand breadth thick, and the brim thereof was wrought like the brim of a cup, with flowers of lilies: it contained two thousand baths.", insight:"Lilies on the brim of a sea of brass; even the washbasin wears beauty."},
{q:"What were the dimensions of each of the ten bases of brass?", options:["Four cubits long, four broad, three high","Six cubits each way","Two cubits each way","Five cubits long, three broad"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:27",verse:"And he made ten bases of brass; four cubits was the length of one base, and four cubits the breadth thereof, and three cubits the height of it.", insight:"Four by four by three, ten times over; God orders the practical things precisely too."},
{q:"What figures were on the borders between the ledges of the bases?", options:["Lions, oxen, and cherubims","Serpents and scorpions","Eagles and stags","Palm trees only"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:29",verse:"And on the borders that were between the ledges were lions, oxen, and cherubims: and upon the ledges there was a base above: and beneath the lions and oxen were certain additions made of thin work.", insight:"Lions, oxen, cherubims on washstand panels; no corner of God's house is beneath His art."},
{q:"How much did each of the ten lavers of brass contain?", options:["Forty baths, each laver four cubits","Twenty baths, each two cubits","A hundred baths, each six cubits","Ten baths, each one cubit"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:38",verse:"Then made he ten lavers of brass: one laver contained forty baths: and every laver was four cubits: and upon every one of the ten bases one laver.", insight:"Forty baths each, ten lavers; God provides washing enough for all His servants."},
{q:"What gold vessels did Solomon make for the house of the LORD?", options:["The altar of gold and the table of gold for the shewbread","A throne of ivory","A crown for the high priest","Trumpets of silver"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 7:48",verse:"And Solomon made all the vessels that pertained unto the house of the LORD: the altar of gold, and the table of gold, whereupon the shewbread was,", insight:"Gold altar, gold table; what touches God's presence is made of the best."}
]},
{n:8, name:"The Dedication Prayer", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 8:27",verse:"But will God indeed dwell on the earth? behold, the heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain thee; how much less this house that I have builded?"}, facts:["Did you know there was nothing in the ark except the two tables of stone which Moses put there at Horeb, when the LORD made the covenant with Israel (1 Kings 8:9)?","Did you know that when the priests came out of the holy place, the cloud filled the house of the LORD, and the glory was so strong the priests could not stand to minister (1 Kings 8:10-11)?","Did you know Solomon offered twenty-two thousand oxen and one hundred and twenty thousand sheep at the dedication, and kept the feast fourteen days, seven and seven (1 Kings 8:63-65)?"], questions:[
{q:"Whom did Solomon assemble to bring up the ark?", options:["The elders of Israel, the heads of the tribes, and the chief of the fathers","Only the priests and Levites","The captains of the army","The merchants of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:1",verse:"Then Solomon assembled the elders of Israel, and all the heads of the tribes, the chief of the fathers of the children of Israel, unto king Solomon in Jerusalem, that they might bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD out of the city of David, which is Zion.", insight:"Elders, heads, fathers; the whole nation gathered, because the ark belonged to all Israel."},
{q:"In what month did all Israel assemble for the feast?", options:["Ethanim, the seventh month","Zif, the second month","Abib, the first month","Bul, the eighth month"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:2",verse:"And all the men of Israel assembled themselves unto king Solomon at the feast in the month Ethanim, which is the seventh month.", insight:"The seventh month, the month of fullness; God times His great days well."},
{q:"Who took up the ark, and what else was brought up with it?", options:["The priests took up the ark, with the tabernacle and all the holy vessels","The Levites carried the ark alone","Solomon bore it on his shoulders","The elders carried it by turns"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:4",verse:"And they brought up the ark of the LORD, and the tabernacle of the congregation, and all the holy vessels that were in the tabernacle, even those did the priests and the Levites bring up.", insight:"Ark, tabernacle, vessels together; nothing holy is left behind when God moves house."},
{q:"Where did the priests set the ark?", options:["In the oracle of the house, the most holy place, under the wings of the cherubims","In the porch before the temple","In the court before the altar","In a chamber of the king's house"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:6",verse:"And the priests brought in the ark of the covenant of the LORD unto his place, into the oracle of the house, to the most holy place, even under the wings of the cherubims.", insight:"Under the cherubims' wings; the ark rests where heaven's guardians spread their covering."},
{q:"What was done with the staves of the ark?", options:["They were drawn out so the ends were seen in the holy place, and there they are unto this day","They were removed and burned","They were overlaid with gold","They were given to the Levites as staves of office"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:8",verse:"And they drew out the staves, that the ends of the staves were seen out in the holy place before the oracle, and they were not seen without: and there they are unto this day.", insight:"The staves stayed ready, ends in view; God's presence is always prepared to move with His people."},
{q:"What was inside the ark?", options:["Nothing save the two tables of stone which Moses put there at Horeb","The rod of Aaron and the pot of manna only","The book of the law written by Moses","Gold, silver, and precious stones"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:9",verse:"There was nothing in the ark save the two tables of stone, which Moses put there at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of the land of Egypt.", insight:"Only the two tables of stone; at the heart of worship is God's word, nothing added."},
{q:"What happened when the priests came out of the holy place?", options:["The cloud filled the house of the LORD, and they could not stand to minister because of the glory","A great wind shook the pillars","Fire fell and consumed the sacrifices","The veil was torn in two"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:11",verse:"So that the priests could not stand to minister because of the cloud: for the glory of the LORD had filled the house of the LORD.", insight:"Glory filled the house till priests could not stand; God's presence outshines all our ministering."},
{q:"Where did Solomon say the LORD would dwell?", options:["In the thick darkness","In the brightest light","On the highest mountain","In the open heavens only"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:12",verse:"Then spake Solomon, The LORD said that he would dwell in thick darkness.", insight:"Thick darkness; God is not afraid of mystery, and reverence begins where sight ends."},
{q:"What did the king do when he turned to the congregation?", options:["He blessed all the congregation of Israel, while they all stood","He commanded them to kneel","He read the law aloud","He offered the first sacrifice himself"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:14",verse:"And the king turned his face about, and blessed all the congregation of Israel: (and all the congregation of Israel stood;)", insight:"The king blessed the people standing; leadership that blesses is leadership that serves."},
{q:"What did God say to David about his desire to build the house?", options:["Thou didst well that it was in thine heart","Thy desire was presumptuous","Another prophet shall build it","Thy son is unworthy of the task"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:18",verse:"And the LORD said unto David my father, Whereas it was in thine heart to build an house unto my name, thou didst well that it was in thine heart.", insight:"God honored the desire though David could not build; He weighs the heart, not only the hands."},
{q:"What did Solomon do as he began his great prayer?", options:["He stood before the altar and spread forth his hands toward heaven","He lay prostrate on the pavement","He lifted up the ark with his own hands","He climbed the steps of the porch"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:22",verse:"And Solomon stood before the altar of the LORD in the presence of all the congregation of Israel, and spread forth his hands toward heaven:", insight:"Hands spread toward heaven; prayer is open-handed before God, holding nothing back."},
{q:"How did Solomon describe God at the start of his prayer?", options:["There is no God like thee, in heaven above or on earth beneath, who keepest covenant and mercy","Thou art a God far off and unknowable","Thou dwellest only in temples made with hands","Thou art a God of war alone"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:23",verse:"And he said, LORD God of Israel, there is no God like thee, in heaven above, or on earth beneath, who keepest covenant and mercy with thy servants that walk before thee with all their heart:", insight:"No God like Thee, keeper of covenant and mercy; prayer begins with who God is, not what we need."},
{q:"What did Solomon confess about God and the house he had built?", options:["The heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain thee; how much less this house","God lives only within these walls","The house is greater than the heaven of heavens","No house on earth can please God"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:27",verse:"But will God indeed dwell on the earth? behold, the heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain thee; how much less this house that I have builded?", insight:"Even heaven cannot contain Him; the wisest builder knows his temple is small beside his God."},
{q:"What did Solomon ask concerning God's eyes and this house?", options:["That His eyes be open toward this house night and day","That He close His eyes to Israel's sins","That He look only on the priests","That He turn His face from the nations"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:29",verse:"That thine eyes may be open toward this house night and day, even toward the place of which thou hast said, My name shall be there: that thou mayest hearken unto the prayer which thy servant shall make toward this place.", insight:"Eyes open night and day; God's watch over His house never sleeps."},
{q:"What did Solomon ask God to do from heaven, His dwelling place?", options:["Hear, and when thou hearest, forgive","Send fire as in the days of Elijah","Strike the enemies at once","Give Israel wealth forever"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:30",verse:"And hearken thou to the supplication of thy servant, and of thy people Israel, when they shall pray toward this place: and hear thou in heaven thy dwelling place: and when thou hearest, forgive.", insight:"Hear and forgive; the king's greatest request was mercy, not might."},
{q:"What did Solomon say about God's knowledge of men?", options:["Thou, even thou only, knowest the hearts of all the children of men","No man knows his own heart","The priests know the hearts of the people","Kings alone understand the heart"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:39",verse:"Then hear thou in heaven thy dwelling place, and forgive, and do, and give to every man according to his ways, whose heart thou knowest; (for thou, even thou only, knowest the hearts of all the children of men;)", insight:"God alone knows every heart; pray honestly, for nothing in you is hidden from Him."},
{q:"Why did Solomon ask God to hear the stranger from a far country?", options:["That all people of the earth may know thy name, and fear thee","That Israel might grow rich by trade","That the stranger might become king","That the nations would fear Israel's army"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:43",verse:"Hear thou in heaven thy dwelling place, and do according to all that the stranger calleth to thee for: that all people of the earth may know thy name, to fear thee, as do thy people Israel; and that they may know that this house, which I have builded, is called by thy name.", insight:"The temple prayer reached beyond Israel; God's house was always meant for all peoples."},
{q:"What humble confession did Solomon make about all men?", options:["There is no man that sinneth not","The righteous never fall","Kings are above sin","Strangers sin more than Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:46",verse:"If they sin against thee, (for there is no man that sinneth not,) and thou be angry with them, and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captives unto the land of the enemy, far or near;", insight:"No man sinneth not; the wisest king began his plea with universal guilt."},
{q:"What did Solomon declare after his prayer was ended?", options:["There hath not failed one word of all his good promise","The temple will stand forever","Israel shall never sin again","The nations will serve Solomon"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:56",verse:"Blessed be the LORD, that hath given rest unto his people Israel, according to all that he promised: there hath not failed one word of all his good promise, which he promised by the hand of Moses his servant.", insight:"Not one word failed; look back over God's promises and count them kept."},
{q:"What was Solomon's charge to the people at the end?", options:["Let your heart therefore be perfect with the LORD our God","Build higher walls around Jerusalem","Offer twice as many sacrifices","Never leave the city of David"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 8:61",verse:"Let your heart therefore be perfect with the LORD our God, to walk in his statutes, and to keep his commandments, as at this day.", insight:"A perfect heart, not a perfect temple; God asks for the inside first."}
]},
{n:9, name:"The LORD's Warning", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 9:3",verse:"And the LORD said unto him, I have heard thy prayer and thy supplication, that thou hast made before me: I have hallowed this house, which thou hast built, to put my name there for ever; and mine eyes and mine heart shall be there perpetually."}, facts:["Did you know the LORD appeared to Solomon a second time, as He had appeared to him at Gibeon, and said, 'mine eyes and mine heart shall be there perpetually' (1 Kings 9:2-3)?","Did you know Solomon gave Hiram twenty cities in Galilee as payment, but when Hiram saw them they pleased him not, and he called the district Cabul (1 Kings 9:11-13)?","Did you know Solomon built a navy of ships at Ezion-geber, on the shore of the Red Sea, which fetched four hundred and twenty talents of gold from Ophir (1 Kings 9:26-28)?"], questions:[
{q:"When did the LORD appear to Solomon the second time?", options:["When he had finished the house of the LORD, the king's house, and all his desire","Before the foundation was laid","During the famine in David's days","After the queen of Sheba departed"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:2",verse:"That the LORD appeared to Solomon the second time, as he had appeared unto him at Gibeon.", insight:"God appeared after the work was done; He meets us in completion as well as in beginning."},
{q:"What did the LORD say He had done with Solomon's prayer?", options:["I have heard thy prayer and thy supplication, and have hallowed this house","Thy prayer was too long to be heard","I will answer only the priests","Thy words were hidden from me"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:3",verse:"And the LORD said unto him, I have heard thy prayer and thy supplication, that thou hast made before me: I have hallowed this house, which thou hast built, to put my name there for ever; and mine eyes and mine heart shall be there perpetually.", insight:"I have heard; before the warning came, the assurance: God listens first, then He speaks."},
{q:"What did God require of Solomon to keep the promise?", options:["To walk before Him as David walked, in integrity of heart","To build a second house in Galilee","To conquer the Philistines","To number all Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:4",verse:"And if thou wilt walk before me, as David thy father walked, in integrity of heart, and in uprightness, to do according to all that I have commanded thee, and wilt keep my statutes and my judgments:", insight:"The promise stood on a walk; blessing follows the obedient heart."},
{q:"How was Solomon to walk if his throne was to be established forever?", options:["As David his father walked, in integrity of heart and uprightness, keeping God's statutes and judgments","By multiplying horses and wives","By building more cities than any king","By exacting heavier tribute"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:4",verse:"And if thou wilt walk before me, as David thy father walked, in integrity of heart, and in uprightness, to do according to all that I have commanded thee, and wilt keep my statutes and my judgments:", insight:"Integrity of heart, uprightness of life; thrones are established by character, not by conquest."},
{q:"What promise about the throne did God renew to Solomon?", options:["There shall not fail thee a man upon the throne of Israel","Thy sons shall rule the whole earth","No enemy shall ever rise","Thy kingdom shall have no end in thy lifetime only"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:5",verse:"Then I will establish the throne of thy kingdom upon Israel for ever, as I promised to David thy father, saying, There shall not fail thee a man upon the throne of Israel.", insight:"A man on the throne forever; God keeps His word to David even when sons will fail it."},
{q:"What would happen if Israel turned to serve other gods?", options:["Israel would be cut off from the land, the house cast out of God's sight, and Israel become a proverb and byword","God would overlook it for David's sake","The temple would be moved to another city","Nothing, for the covenant was unconditional"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:7",verse:"Then will I cut off Israel out of the land which I have given them; and this house, which I have hallowed for my name, will I cast out of my sight; and Israel shall be a proverb and a byword among all people:", insight:"Cast out of His sight, a proverb and byword; privilege never protects persistent unfaithfulness."},
{q:"What would passersby say when they saw the ruined house?", options:["Why hath the LORD done thus unto this land, and to this house?","Who built this desolation?","Blessed be the stones that remain","Let us rebuild it quickly"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:8",verse:"And at this house, which is high, every one that passeth by it shall be astonished, and shall hiss; and they shall say, Why hath the LORD done thus unto this land, and to this house?", insight:"They would hiss and ask why; a fallen testimony preaches its own sad sermon."},
{q:"What answer would be given for the ruin?", options:["Because they forsook the LORD their God, and took hold upon other gods","Because their enemies were too strong","Because the kings were poor","Because the priests fled"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:9",verse:"And they shall answer, Because they forsook the LORD their God, who brought forth their fathers out of the land of Egypt, and have taken hold upon other gods, and have worshipped them, and served them: therefore hath the LORD brought upon them all this evil.", insight:"Because they forsook the Lord; every ruin has a reason, and God names it plainly."},
{q:"At the end of how many years had Solomon built the two houses?", options:["Twenty years","Seven years","Thirteen years","Forty years"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:10",verse:"And it came to pass at the end of twenty years, when Solomon had built the two houses, the house of the LORD, and the king’s house,", insight:"Twenty years, seven plus thirteen; God counts the whole work, temple and palace together."},
{q:"What did Solomon give Hiram king of Tyre?", options:["Twenty cities in the land of Galilee","A hundred talents of silver","The city of Joppa","Ships of the navy"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:11",verse:"(Now Hiram the king of Tyre had furnished Solomon with cedar trees and fir trees, and with gold, according to all his desire,) that then king Solomon gave Hiram twenty cities in the land of Galilee.", insight:"Twenty cities for cedar, fir, and gold; even kings pay their debts, or try to."},
{q:"How did Hiram find the cities Solomon gave him?", options:["They pleased him not","They delighted him greatly","He refused to look at them","He sold them at once"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:12",verse:"And Hiram came out from Tyre to see the cities which Solomon had given him; and they pleased him not.", insight:"They pleased him not; a gift that disappoints is a debt still unpaid."},
{q:"What did Hiram call the cities, and what did the name mean for them?", options:["The land of Cabul, and so they are called unto this day","The land of Promise","The cities of David","The villages of Tyre"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:13",verse:"And he said, What cities are these which thou hast given me, my brother? And he called them the land of Cabul unto this day.", insight:"Cabul, a name of displeasure remembered for generations; reputations outlive transactions."},
{q:"How much gold did Hiram send to the king?", options:["Sixscore talents of gold","Forty talents","A thousand talents","Ten talents"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:14",verse:"And Hiram sent to the king sixscore talents of gold.", insight:"Sixscore talents sent back; even a disappointed friend can act generously."},
{q:"For what was the levy raised that Solomon imposed?", options:["To build the house of the LORD, his own house, Millo, the wall of Jerusalem, Hazor, Megiddo, and Gezer","To pay tribute to Pharaoh","To hire an army of mercenaries","To build ships only"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:15",verse:"And this is the reason of the levy which king Solomon raised; for to build the house of the LORD, and his own house, and Millo, and the wall of Jerusalem, and Hazor, and Megiddo, and Gezer.", insight:"Temple, palace, walls, and cities; great building programs are paid for by somebody."},
{q:"How did Pharaoh's daughter come to possess Gezer?", options:["Pharaoh took Gezer, burnt it, slew the Canaanites, and gave it as a present to his daughter, Solomon's wife","She conquered it herself","Solomon bought it with gold","It was her dowry from Tyre"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:16",verse:"For Pharaoh king of Egypt had gone up, and taken Gezer, and burnt it with fire, and slain the Canaanites that dwelt in the city, and given it for a present unto his daughter, Solomon’s wife.", insight:"A burnt city for a wedding gift; the politics of kings touches the lives of common people."},
{q:"Which peoples did Solomon put under tribute of bondservice?", options:["The Amorites, Hittites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites left in the land","The Egyptians","The men of Judah","The tribe of Levi"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:21",verse:"Their children that were left after them in the land, whom the children of Israel also were not able utterly to destroy, upon those did Solomon levy a tribute of bondservice unto this day.", insight:"The remaining nations served under tribute; unfinished conquests become lasting burdens."},
{q:"What did Solomon refuse to make of the children of Israel?", options:["Bondmen; they were men of war, servants, princes, captains, and rulers","Priests","Farmers","Merchants"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:22",verse:"But of the children of Israel did Solomon make no bondmen: but they were men of war, and his servants, and his princes, and his captains, and rulers of his chariots, and his horsemen.", insight:"No bondmen of Israel; God's people serve as free men, not as slaves."},
{q:"How many chief officers bore rule over Solomon's work?", options:["Five hundred and fifty","A thousand","Three hundred","Seventy"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:23",verse:"These were the chief of the officers that were over Solomon’s work, five hundred and fifty, which bare rule over the people that wrought in the work.", insight:"Five hundred and fifty overseers; great works need many hands, and hands need oversight."},
{q:"How often in a year did Solomon offer upon the altar?", options:["Three times in a year, burnt offerings and peace offerings, and burnt incense","Once, at the feast of unleavened bread","Seven times, at every new moon","Twelve times, month by month"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:25",verse:"And three times in a year did Solomon offer burnt offerings and peace offerings upon the altar which he built unto the LORD, and he burnt incense upon the altar that was before the LORD. So he finished the house.", insight:"Three times a year, without fail; rhythm in worship keeps the heart from drifting."},
{q:"How much gold did the navy fetch from Ophir?", options:["Four hundred and twenty talents","Six hundred talents","A hundred and twenty talents","Fifty talents"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 9:28",verse:"And they came to Ophir, and fetched from thence gold, four hundred and twenty talents, and brought it to king Solomon.", insight:"Four hundred and twenty talents from Ophir; God opens distant shores to a praying king."}
]},
{n:10, name:"The Queen of Sheba", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 10:24",verse:"And all the earth sought to Solomon, to hear his wisdom, which God had put in his heart."}, facts:["Did you know the queen of Sheba confessed, 'the half was not told me: thy wisdom and prosperity exceedeth the fame which I heard' (1 Kings 10:7)?","Did you know her gift of spices was so great that there never came again such abundance of spices as the queen of Sheba gave to Solomon (1 Kings 10:10)?","Did you know six hundred threescore and six talents of gold came to Solomon in one year, and in his days silver was nothing accounted of (1 Kings 10:14, 10:21)?"], questions:[
{q:"Why did the queen of Sheba come to Solomon?", options:["She heard of his fame concerning the name of the LORD, and came to prove him with hard questions","She came to marry him","She came to buy cedar for her own temple","She fled from war in her own land"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:1",verse:"And when the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon concerning the name of the LORD, she came to prove him with hard questions.", insight:"She came concerning the name of the LORD; true fame points past the man to his God."},
{q:"With what did the queen come to Jerusalem?", options:["A very great train, camels bearing spices, very much gold, and precious stones","A small band of servants in secret","An army of chariots","Only her household and her counselors"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:2",verse:"And she came to Jerusalem with a very great train, with camels that bare spices, and very much gold, and precious stones: and when she was come to Solomon, she communed with him of all that was in her heart.", insight:"Camels heavy with spices and gold; seekers of wisdom come prepared to honor it."},
{q:"What happened when she communed with Solomon of all that was in her heart?", options:["Solomon told her all her questions; nothing was hid from the king","He refused to answer her riddles","He sent her to his counselors","He answered only half"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:3",verse:"And Solomon told her all her questions: there was not any thing hid from the king, which he told her not.", insight:"Nothing hid from the king; wisdom given by God has an answer for every honest question."},
{q:"What overwhelmed the queen when she saw Solomon's house and court?", options:["The meat of his table, his servants, ministers, apparel, cupbearers, and his ascent to the house of the LORD, till there was no more spirit in her","The size of his army","The height of the temple walls","The number of his wives"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:5",verse:"And the meat of his table, and the sitting of his servants, and the attendance of his ministers, and their apparel, and his cupbearers, and his ascent by which he went up unto the house of the LORD; there was no more spirit in her.", insight:"No more spirit in her; true greatness leaves visitors breathless, not boastful."},
{q:"What did she say about the report she had heard in her own land?", options:["It was a true report of his acts and his wisdom","It was greatly exaggerated","It was a lie of the merchants","It told only of his riches"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:6",verse:"And she said to the king, It was a true report that I heard in mine own land of thy acts and of thy wisdom.", insight:"A true report; the half may be untold, but what is told should be true."},
{q:"What did the queen confess about her former unbelief?", options:["I believed not until mine eyes had seen it, and the half was not told me","I believed everything at once","I still doubt what I have seen","I believed the merchants more than the king"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:7",verse:"Howbeit I believed not the words, until I came, and mine eyes had seen it: and, behold, the half was not told me: thy wisdom and prosperity exceedeth the fame which I heard.", insight:"The half was not told me; come and see for yourself before you judge God's work."},
{q:"Whom did the queen call happy?", options:["His men and servants, who stand continually before him and hear his wisdom","The rich merchants of Sheba","The builders of the temple","The priests alone"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:8",verse:"Happy are thy men, happy are these thy servants, which stand continually before thee, and that hear thy wisdom.", insight:"Happy are they that hear his wisdom; nearness to wisdom is itself a blessing."},
{q:"Why did she say God made Solomon king?", options:["Because the LORD loved Israel forever, to do judgment and justice","Because Solomon was the strongest warrior","Because David had many sons","Because the people demanded it"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:9",verse:"Blessed be the LORD thy God, which delighted in thee, to set thee on the throne of Israel: because the LORD loved Israel for ever, therefore made he thee king, to do judgment and justice.", insight:"To do judgment and justice; a foreign queen saw what Israel sometimes forgot, that the throne exists for righteousness."},
{q:"What did the queen give to Solomon?", options:["An hundred and twenty talents of gold, very great store of spices, and precious stones","A thousand chariots","Her own crown","Cities on the Red Sea"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:10",verse:"And she gave the king an hundred and twenty talents of gold, and of spices very great store, and precious stones: there came no more such abundance of spices as these which the queen of Sheba gave to king Solomon.", insight:"A hundred and twenty talents of gold; generosity answers wisdom with open hands."},
{q:"What did Hiram's navy bring from Ophir besides gold?", options:["Great plenty of almug trees and precious stones","Silver and bronze","Horses and chariots","Wheat and oil"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:11",verse:"And the navy also of Hiram, that brought gold from Ophir, brought in from Ophir great plenty of almug trees, and precious stones.", insight:"Almug trees from Ophir; God's provision arrives from places you have never seen."},
{q:"What was made from the almug trees?", options:["Pillars for the house of the LORD and the king's house, and harps and psalteries for singers","Ships for the navy","A throne for the queen","Doors for the temple"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:12",verse:"And the king made of the almug trees pillars for the house of the LORD, and for the king’s house, harps also and psalteries for singers: there came no such almug trees, nor were seen unto this day.", insight:"Pillars and harps from one wood; the same gift serves both worship and work."},
{q:"What did Solomon give the queen of Sheba?", options:["All her desire, whatsoever she asked, besides his royal bounty, and she returned to her own country","Only safe passage home","Half his treasury","A fleet of ships"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:13",verse:"And king Solomon gave unto the queen of Sheba all her desire, whatsoever she asked, beside that which Solomon gave her of his royal bounty. So she turned and went to her own country, she and her servants.", insight:"All her desire, plus royal bounty; true wisdom gives more than is asked."},
{q:"How much gold came to Solomon in one year?", options:["Six hundred threescore and six talents of gold","A thousand talents","Four hundred talents","Two hundred talents"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:14",verse:"Now the weight of gold that came to Solomon in one year was six hundred threescore and six talents of gold.", insight:"Six hundred sixty-six talents in a year; wealth flowed to Solomon, and would one day flow away from his heart."},
{q:"How many targets of beaten gold did Solomon make, and how much gold went to each?", options:["Two hundred targets, six hundred shekels of gold to each","A hundred targets, three hundred shekels each","Three hundred targets, a thousand shekels each","Fifty targets, a hundred shekels each"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:16",verse:"And king Solomon made two hundred targets of beaten gold: six hundred shekels of gold went to one target.", insight:"Two hundred targets of beaten gold; even shields of war were gilded in the days of peace."},
{q:"How many shields of beaten gold, and where were they put?", options:["Three hundred shields, three pound of gold each, put in the house of the forest of Lebanon","Two hundred shields, kept in the temple","A hundred shields, hung on the city wall","Five hundred shields, stored in Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:17",verse:"And he made three hundred shields of beaten gold; three pound of gold went to one shield: and the king put them in the house of the forest of Lebanon.", insight:"Three hundred shields in the forest house; glory stored up is glory that can be carried away."},
{q:"Of what was Solomon's great throne made?", options:["Ivory, overlaid with the best gold","Solid silver","Cedar overlaid with brass","Marble and onyx"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:18",verse:"Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with the best gold.", insight:"Ivory and best gold; earthly thrones shine brightest just before they fade."},
{q:"How many lions stood upon the six steps of the throne?", options:["Twelve lions, on either side of the six steps","Six lions, one per step","Two lions beside the seat","Twenty four lions around the base"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:20",verse:"And twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other upon the six steps: there was not the like made in any kingdom.", insight:"Twelve lions on six steps; the throne of Judah's king guarded by the tribe's own emblem."},
{q:"What was said of silver in the days of Solomon?", options:["It was nothing accounted of","It was rarer than gold","It was forbidden in the palace","It was used only for the temple"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:21",verse:"And all king Solomon’s drinking vessels were of gold, and all the vessels of the house of the forest of Lebanon were of pure gold; none were of silver: it was nothing accounted of in the days of Solomon.", insight:"Silver nothing accounted of; when gold is common, men forget what true wealth is."},
{q:"What did the navy of Tharshish bring once in three years?", options:["Gold, silver, ivory, apes, and peacocks","Spices and perfumes only","Timber for building","Grain for the storehouses"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:22",verse:"For the king had at sea a navy of Tharshish with the navy of Hiram: once in three years came the navy of Tharshish, bringing gold, and silver, ivory, and apes, and peacocks.", insight:"Apes and peacocks with the gold; prosperity brings curiosities as well as treasure."},
{q:"How many chariots and horsemen did Solomon gather?", options:["A thousand and four hundred chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen","Four thousand chariots and forty thousand horsemen","Seven hundred chariots and seven thousand horsemen","No chariots, only footmen"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 10:26",verse:"And Solomon gathered together chariots and horsemen: and he had a thousand and four hundred chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen, whom he bestowed in the cities for chariots, and with the king at Jerusalem.", insight:"Chariots and horsemen multiplied; the king was already reaching for what God had warned against."}
]}
]);
